<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

	<!--
		The soldier beetle's armament (2026-10-01, archive/CASTES-PLAN.md phase 5). The mockup asks for "one
		of ripper blades, a charger claw or a horn", and all three are VRE Insector genes that
		already exist, so this def is the list and Source/Insects/BeetleArmament.cs is the pick - the
		same shape the castes' body colours use (archive/HANDOFF.md §5.13): the register is XML, the code
		never names a weapon (corrected 2026-10-03: see below).

		VRE's charger claws is NOT a weapon. It grants the ability VFEI2_BreacherCharge_Colonists and
		a work-speed penalty, and no attack at all. Every real option grants a hediff carrying a
		HediffCompProperties_VerbGiver, and those verbs are the only attack a beetle has, because her
		race carried no tools of its own. A beetle who rolled charger claws therefore had no
		melee verbs at all: the log read "has no available melee attack, ... verbList= bodyVerbs=",
		and another mod's postfix threw a NullReferenceException on every job scan. The girtablilu is
		unaffected - she carries VRE_ChargerClaws *and* her own pincer tools, so the charge is a
		bonus to her rather than her weapon - and she keeps them (user's call, 2026-10-03: that was the intended design), because those pincers are the floor underneath them. Her own fists are back since 2026-10-03 (user's call), so an option that grants no attack is now a lost preference rather than a girl left defenceless - and the armament gene is still what she reaches for.

		Why a gene and not the race: archive/CASTES-PLAN.md §0 decision 11 emptied her race's tool list so
		the weapon gene owns the weapon, which is also the mantis's shape (archive/HANDOFF.md §5.18). Nothing
		is lost by that - all three options grant a hediff with a
		`HediffCompProperties_VerbGiver`, not a race tool, so she attacks with the same ripper-blades,
		mandibles or horn as any VRE insectoid. That is what made the list load-bearing rather than cosmetic: with no race tools underneath her, an option that grants no attack left her with nothing to swing.

		Why this gene is visible at all: a roll is invisible until it lands, so her xenotype lists the
		roll and her gene page shows what it gave her. One of the three appears beside this one.

		The cost sits on the weapon genes themselves - this wrapper is free of metabolic cost and
		charges one complexity point, so she is never billed twice for her armament. Out of the
		random gene sets for the same reason the quarrels are: a trader's genepack should not hand a
		stranger a beetle's weapon.

		Its icon is core's claw art for now - see the iconPath below - and hand art at
		Textures/UI/Icons/Genes/Gene_BeetleArmament replaces it when it exists.
	-->
	<GeneDef>
		<defName>PMM_Gene_BeetleArmament</defName>
		<label>beetle armament</label>
		<description>Her carapace grows one of three killing tools - a pair of ripper-blades, charger claws, or a heavy horn - and which one is hers is settled when she is born.</description>
		<geneClass>PMM_Insects.Gene_BeetleArmament</geneClass>
		<!-- Core's claw art, borrowed while hers is undrawn: it is the closest thing in the family
		     to "a weapon grown out of her body", it is already loaded (PMM.Core is a dependency),
		     and she never carries the gene it belongs to, so nothing on her gene page repeats.
		     Hand art at Textures/UI/Icons/Genes/Gene_BeetleArmament replaces it when it exists. -->
		<iconPath>UI/Icons/Genes/PMM_Gene_MamonoClaws</iconPath>
		<displayCategory>Miscellaneous</displayCategory>
		<displayOrderInCategory>1005</displayOrderInCategory>
		<biostatMet>-2</biostatMet>
		<biostatCpx>1</biostatCpx>
		<canGenerateInGeneSet>false</canGenerateInGeneSet>
		<modExtensions>
			<li Class="PMM_Insects.BeetleArmamentRoll">
				<armaments>
					<!-- The three she rolls between, and mandibles stands where the mockup's "charger claw" stood. They exclude each other's ground -
					     VRE_MegaspiderHorns excludes the Headbone cosmetic tag, the other two carry
					     their own lists - so the roll must be their only writer, and
					     BeetleArmament.Roll removes whichever one she already has before it adds
					     the new one. -->
					<li>VRE_RipperBlades</li>
					<li>VRE_InsectMandibles</li>
					<li>VRE_MegaspiderHorns</li>
				</armaments>
				<!-- Names she may already carry from a version of this list that predates the correction
				     above. BeetleArmament.Roll removes these too, so a beetle who rolled charger claws
				     before 2026-10-03 loses it and picks a real weapon. -->
				<retiredArmaments>
					<li>VRE_ChargerClaws</li>
				</retiredArmaments>
			</li>
		</modExtensions>
	</GeneDef>

</Defs>
